      "writtenOn": "2023-04-11T15:52:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "SMCCC is the specification that underpins all communication via SMC/HVCs. MMIO guard is just one user of it. Other users should not have to include MMIO guard to get SMCCC.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 19,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 19,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "921d92a2ad382060c3aca253b2dda06896d9902b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7c309bd3_b56f10d2",
        "filename": "pvmfw/src/hvc.rs",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 19,
      "author": {
        "id": 1882526
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-11T16:15:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The pKVM HVCs being a somewhat standard vendor hypervisor interface, they could arguably also be moved under their own `libpsci` module (e.g. `psci::vendor::kvm`).",
      "parentUuid": "90a17beb_c88b7a0b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 19,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 19,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "921d92a2ad382060c3aca253b2dda06896d9902b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1fd08ab7_bea56b74",
        "filename": "pvmfw/src/hvc.rs",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 19,
      "author": {
        "id": 1958315
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-12T10:26:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "libpsci provides the base hvc64() call that is used for psci, mmio_guard and trng. Among them, psci only needs the raw hvc64 call, but mmio_guard and trng add another layer of Error and checked call on top of that. Currently users mostly need the Error/Result from mmio_guard::smccc and trng, it\u0027s a bit weird to put all these in psci.",
      "parentUuid": "7c309bd3_b56f10d2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 19,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 19,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "921d92a2ad382060c3aca253b2dda06896d9902b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6de8e2a8_1164965f",
        "filename": "pvmfw/src/hvc.rs",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 19,
      "author": {
        "id": 1059815
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-12T11:45:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We need to change `libpsci` - it should not provide `hvc64`.\n\nIn the meantime, this looks almost right. Sorry for being pedantic, but I think we should also extract `smccc.rs` from `libpkvm` into `libsmccc`. SMCCC is not a pKVM concept and, for example, libraries providing HVCs for other hypervisors should not need to depend on `libpkvm`.",
      "parentUuid": "1fd08ab7_bea56b74",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 19,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 19,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "921d92a2ad382060c3aca253b2dda06896d9902b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
